In order to make things work smoothly, the module has to have its own namespace, and a namespace that is closed.<p>D also has an `alias` feature, where you can do things like:<p><pre><code>    alias Q = abc.T;
</code></pre>
where from then on, `abc.T` can be referred to simply as `Q`. This also eliminates a large chunk of purpose behind the preprocessor.
